    "body": "## Problem\r\n`gQ` restores cleared multicursors but leaves the primary cursor at its current position instead of restoring it to where it was when the multicursors were cleared.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nSnapshot the position of the primary cursor when multicursors are cleared and restore primary cursor to that position on `gQ`.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42004#discussion_r4055165633"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/42004"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/4055165633"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I'll defer to people with merge perms on this, but could this be toggleable with a boolean flag? Then I could set:\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gQ\", function()\n  require(\"vim._core.mcursor\").restore(false)\nend)\n```\nSince I prefer the previous behavior more. If not, I could just reimplement it myself - but thought I'd ask.",
